Support legacy OpenGL 2.x contexts (GLSL 1.20), e.g. on Mac OS X 10.6.

- imgl3w loader: accept GL 2.x, parse GL_VERSION when GL_MAJOR_VERSION
  is not available instead of failing the loader initialisation.
- imgui_impl_opengl3: only use vertex array objects on GL 3.0+ / ES 3.0+,
  otherwise render with the default vertex array and back up the vertex
  attribute state (the existing ES 2.0 path).
- macOS: if a 3.2 core context cannot be created, retry with a legacy
  context, use "#version 120" shaders for it, and lower the minimum
  OpenGL version check to 2.0.

